# Normalize all text files to LF in the repository and in every checkout, on
# all platforms. This repo is developed on Linux/macOS (already LF), so this is
# zero-churn — it simply prevents Windows checkouts (core.autocrlf=true) from
# rewriting text to CRLF.
#
# Why this matters: the newt-eval bundled cases store unified diffs in
# `cases/**/case.toml`, which are fed verbatim to `git apply --check`. With
# CRLF line endings git rejects them as "corrupt patch" (the `\r` becomes part
# of the patch body). Rust source, fixtures, and scripts are all LF-sensitive
# here, so we pin LF rather than chase per-file tolerance.
#
# `text=auto` still auto-detects binary files (NUL bytes) and leaves them alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
